
C1  small-z expansion of F_n (general n)
  [PASS] F_n = (2n/3) z^(3/2) - (n(n+1)/4) z^2 + ...
         measured : coeff z^(3/2) = 2*n/3,  coeff z^2 = n*(-n - 1)/4
         threshold: must equal 2n/3 and -n(n+1)/4 identically in n
  [PASS] leading term is NON-ANALYTIC (half-integer power), no z^1 term
         measured : F_n(z) ~ z^(3/2); the coefficient of z^1 is 0 for every n
         threshold: F'(0) = mu(0) = 0  =>  no quadratic kinetic term at the origin

C2  the one dimensionless invariant a bound would have to fix
  [PASS] after fixing a0, exactly ONE free number distinguishes the members
