  [PASS] so the AADNR premise (a gapped, weakly coupled, Lorentz-invariant vacuum with an analytic s-expansion) is absent, for every n
         measured : the obstruction is n-independent: F'(0)=0 holds for all n>0
         threshold: positivity bounds are not violated here -- they are inapplicable

C4  the AADNR sign test on the surviving analytic structure
  [PASS] F'' > 0 for every member and every Y (so P'' < 0: the forbidden sign)
